        "progression_name": "Sampling an Analog Image: Challenges A&B"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5ebd1456-2b47-4055-8044-41e058b7f89a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a896032f-052e-4a89-9bbd-78b726bb890a"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "47d919d1-88c1-4c4d-b79c-8fe9d2312332",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 5 to answer the checking for understanding question.",
        "progression_name": "Check Your Undertanding",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use this level to check whether students can decode bits into rows of pixels, explain what determines an image's shape, and explain that a 0 or a 1 only means black or white because of an agreed rule."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "47d919d1-88c1-4c4d-b79c-8fe9d2312332",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a896032f-052e-4a89-9bbd-78b726bb890a"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "090553fe-4804-4932-bd2b-2142002d9c93",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Check Your Understanding"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "090553fe-4804-4932-bd2b-2142002d9c93",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a896032f-052e-4a89-9bbd-78b726bb890a"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e0d54330-87fb-4bd2-8b22-cf4f9ff04ad9",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e0d54330-87fb-4bd2-8b22-cf4f9ff04ad9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ad47d929-12bc-4cef-b090-93962bc55b0d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5f8896a8-9f98-4bf8-95a0-bd9143bb2584",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day and give students a moment to just think about what they learned today."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5f8896a8-9f98-4bf8-95a0-bd9143bb2584",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ad47d929-12bc-4cef-b090-93962bc55b0d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3c94c837-2492-4d54-873b-231cfb99b089",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What are the pros and cons of using smaller squares?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** We want students to start seeing that the choices we make when we represent a picture with bits have trade-offs. Some key points to draw out from students:\n- **Pros:** The picture looks smoother, clearer, and closer to the original. It is a little easier to decide whether each square should be black or white.\n- **Cons:** More bits are needed (192 instead of 48). It took longer to enter in the widget. It still doesn't look exactly like the original. Some squares still had both black and white, so a choice had to be made."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3c94c837-2492-4d54-873b-231cfb99b089",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ad47d929-12bc-4cef-b090-93962bc55b0d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "477f324a-792b-4042-a9ea-08ecacddc3ee",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *How many different shades of the color blue can you name?*\n- *How many do you think there are in total?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Start with having students name shades, but quickly transition to how many they think exist altogether. The goal here is to have students begin to wonder if computers can represent all of the vast shades of colors in our world. This should be a quick discussion. You can move on as soon as this point is made."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "477f324a-792b-4042-a9ea-08ecacddc3ee",
        "lesson_activity.key": "590c8ce0-c735-4392-a940-84e0d08511a1"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "530782f7-229c-4e6a-a9c2-b6377bff8aa3",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "530782f7-229c-4e6a-a9c2-b6377bff8aa3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "590c8ce0-c735-4392-a940-84e0d08511a1"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "da964c55-3c23-44b0-9436-6fa913214212",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "da964c55-3c23-44b0-9436-6fa913214212",
        "lesson_activity.key": "590c8ce0-c735-4392-a940-84e0d08511a1"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9497ba30-941c-4c60-b177-ab3122708fd1",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students use the pixelation widget to build colors from groups of red, green, and blue bits, and see that more bits per pixel means more shades.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Pixelation Widget: Color"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9497ba30-941c-4c60-b177-ab3122708fd1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "23a16b96-d62b-468c-a95c-4825b74b7dbe",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Last lesson, each pixel used 1 bit, so it could only be black or white. Today you'll use groups of bits to control red, green, and blue light, and see how many colors you can make as you add more bits. After each level, check your work with your partner.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "23a16b96-d62b-468c-a95c-4825b74b7dbe",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "000b5b7f-5e78-48d6-a9e3-6be979f7416d",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete the challenges on Lesson 10, Levels 1 - 5.\n- **Levels 1-2:** Students should type in a unique 3-bit code for each pixel, producing 8 different colors.\n- **Levels 3-4:** Students make four different shades of blue, followed by four different shades of green, using 6 bits per pixel. The red row is already done for them.\n- **Level 5:** This time, students use 9 bits per pixel. They will make 8 different shades of green and 8 different shades of blue (the red row is done for them).",
        "progression_name": "Pixelation Widget: Color",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "**Levels 2, 4, and 5:** The directions are written in so that students who are color-blind do not need to be able to distinguish between colors to be able to complete the task. That being said, students who are color-blind may not be able to visually check their work in the same way as other students. You can suggest that students who are color-blind ask a partner to check their work at the end of each of these levels."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "000b5b7f-5e78-48d6-a9e3-6be979f7416d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9269dae0-99c5-49dc-89cb-d28e80e34f86",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Notice what you just did. You typed bits, and a color appeared. Keep that in mind, because we'll come back to what sits between those two things.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9269dae0-99c5-49dc-89cb-d28e80e34f86",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2a1ef245-6c4f-46de-ae15-dc26f0cf18c4",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Regroup the class for levels 6-7 and direct everyone to the images on the slides."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2a1ef245-6c4f-46de-ae15-dc26f0cf18c4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "03ff6fa6-2a38-4949-8074-5404bc57c81d",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Look at the grids on these images. Each square would become one pixel, and the whole square gets just one color. Smaller squares mean more pixels, and more pixels mean more bits.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "03ff6fa6-2a38-4949-8074-5404bc57c81d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "86ea15e3-601b-46b6-8c92-ed088590ed71",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that Level 6 contains samples of various color gradients. Students should choose a section from one of the images, try to take a sampling using the widget on level 6 as a support, and attempt to reproduce the sample gradient as best they can on Level 7."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "86ea15e3-601b-46b6-8c92-ed088590ed71",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "939a9022-9693-4e0b-b94b-0f4edd2b4019",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students sample a section of a gradient and match it with the widget, choosing how many bits per pixel to use, to see how a scene becomes pixels and how more bits give a closer match.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete the challenges on Lesson 10, Levels 6-7.\n- **Levels 6-7:** Level 6 contains samples of various color gradients. Students should choose a section from one of the images, try to take a sampling using the widget on level 6 as a support, and attempt to reproduce the sample gradient as best they can on Level 7.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Color Sampling",
        "progression_name": "Color Sampling",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "The widget on Level 6 is meant to help students visualize different sampling frequencies, just like the different grids on the last page of the activity guide from the previous lesson. Students should make their own attempt at matching one of these images using the widget on Level 7.\n\n**Levels 6 and 7:** It is recommended that students who are color-blind choose Image 4, the black and white gradient, since they do not need to distinguish colors to match it."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "939a9022-9693-4e0b-b94b-0f4edd2b4019",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "dfc28d91-de69-411c-9373-0fcb382aa40f",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Color Sampling"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "dfc28d91-de69-411c-9373-0fcb382aa40f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "22a356cd-663c-470c-ba89-e21d8696bc1d",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to Lesson 10, Level 8 and 9 to answer the checking for understanding questions.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Check for Understanding",
        "progression_name": "Check Your Understanding",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use Levels 8 and 9 to check whether students can explain how groups of bits set the red, green, and blue levels of a pixel, name layers of abstraction between bits and a displayed image, and describe what each layer lets a user ignore."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "22a356cd-663c-470c-ba89-e21d8696bc1d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "134853de-ed83-451f-9ecd-12439c04caf0"
      }
    },
