    },
    {
      "key": "bea986fc-736f-4bf7-849d-7c6f5be19941",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Show the example. Students vote and defend with a partner."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bea986fc-736f-4bf7-849d-7c6f5be19941",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "31a9657a-8ab4-4198-ba90-b0b4ed776aa3",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Show the example. Students vote and defend with a partner.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "This one is often confusing since the AI enhanced real content instead of creating something new. Let that tension surface in the discussion."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "31a9657a-8ab4-4198-ba90-b0b4ed776aa3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "73abba32-3574-4ff8-b89c-cd19d82bebf9",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *Which examples were easy calls? Which were hard?*\n- *What made the difference?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Surface that stakes, audience, and intent affect whether disclosure feels necessary. Connect back to the attribution and licensing ideas from the direct instruction."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "73abba32-3574-4ff8-b89c-cd19d82bebf9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b30422f4-bd0f-45d3-abfd-e2ff2570c993",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Investigate how different AI disclosure labels affect trust, and what information a badge does and doesn't communicate.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Put students into groups of 2-3.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each group a copy of the Media Investigation Guide.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "What’s Behind the AI Badge?"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b30422f4-bd0f-45d3-abfd-e2ff2570c993",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a5c50c8a-8a04-4be8-9de6-ee574cfb7cd7",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** In small groups, students examine social media posts with different disclosure labels. Using the Media Investigation Guide, groups answer what the badge tells them, what it doesn't tell them, whether it increases or decreases trust, whether they'd verify before sharing, and whether their decision would change with no label."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a5c50c8a-8a04-4be8-9de6-ee574cfb7cd7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f210fb2b-fa10-4181-bc13-2cc3d49dbe66",
      "position": 14,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What did you notice about how different labels affected your trust?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Different disclosure systems communicate different amounts of information. A badge alone doesn't guarantee accuracy or trustworthiness."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f210fb2b-fa10-4181-bc13-2cc3d49dbe66",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a617e969-b783-492e-84cb-eef1e607032d",
      "position": 15,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that realistic AI media, including deepfakes, can mislead audiences if shared without context."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a617e969-b783-492e-84cb-eef1e607032d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a81032fb-c2d0-49f3-90e7-afd73a8dd0f8",
      "position": 16,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that responsible publishing includes verifying information, disclosing AI use when appropriate, respecting licensing requirements, and considering potential harm before sharing."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a81032fb-c2d0-49f3-90e7-afd73a8dd0f8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f601cf0f-fe4a-4a3d-b183-1ea48360ce15",
      "position": 17,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Step into the role of a content reviewer and apply the same decision-making process across multiple types of media before deciding whether each is ready to publish.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each group a Publication Decision Guide and a media folder.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Ready to Publish?"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f601cf0f-fe4a-4a3d-b183-1ea48360ce15",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d8637291-b6d7-4189-90ef-9fe059ee3ab5",
      "position": 18,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** In small groups, students use the Publication Decision Guide to evaluate every item in the folder before deciding whether it is ready to publish. Groups justify each decision and explain which safeguards they applied."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d8637291-b6d7-4189-90ef-9fe059ee3ab5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e9e100cd-7bed-4435-939c-75a72d752873",
      "position": 19,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which item was hardest to decide on? Why?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Different media types raise different safeguards. A photo needs less scrutiny than a deepfake, and a Creative Commons work needs attribution even though it wasn't made with AI."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e9e100cd-7bed-4435-939c-75a72d752873",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5aff6597-23c5-497f-a270-b911f70ed00d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d9880ed0-76cd-4c78-93ac-cdad7f8d378a",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d9880ed0-76cd-4c78-93ac-cdad7f8d378a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "00c69a9b-15d6-4bb3-ac4e-76ce28851aec"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ac0bad98-2dd2-40b9-8880-249c94df191d",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day and give students a moment to just think about what they learned today."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ac0bad98-2dd2-40b9-8880-249c94df191d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "00c69a9b-15d6-4bb3-ac4e-76ce28851aec"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a6b15c50-21e6-43ea-830c-a6fae31c702b",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a6b15c50-21e6-43ea-830c-a6fae31c702b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "00c69a9b-15d6-4bb3-ac4e-76ce28851aec"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b1f81caf-7765-466c-8791-1b3e6c579713",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students discover, through voting on real messages, that a confidence score is not the same as being correct — and that catching what the bot misses takes a human who actually reads for tone and context. This is exactly how AI moderation fails in the real world: missing slang it was never trained on.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the scenario. Explain that students are acting as admins for a large gaming Discord community whose AI moderation bot has flagged four messages, each with a toxicity score and a suggested action. Clarify that the toxicity score is how confident the bot is, not a fact about the message — a high score just means the bot is sure, not that it's right."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b1f81caf-7765-466c-8791-1b3e6c579713",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e94b3792-d9cd-4f61-bb3e-0048f8195c5e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the three-part checklist. Tell students that before deciding on any flagged message, they run it through Tone, Context, and Stakes.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Tone might be sarcasm read as an insult, Context might be a long-time member versus a brand-new account, and Stakes might be a joke that could still get someone temporarily banned."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e94b3792-d9cd-4f61-bb3e-0048f8195c5e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7073f795-0088-4933-a6fa-052f7b5ecba5",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** For each message, students vote with a hand signal: thumbs up to approve the bot's action, thumbs down to override it, or sideways to escalate to a human moderator."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7073f795-0088-4933-a6fa-052f7b5ecba5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a555d755-782e-4cc8-92a9-001f95c1ab8e",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the first message aloud, then have students vote by hand signal: approve, override, or escalate. Call on a couple students to share a reason before revealing the next message."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a555d755-782e-4cc8-92a9-001f95c1ab8e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "345e2fbf-afae-4447-b70d-a04705d78ef8",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the second message aloud, then have students vote by hand signal: approve, override, or escalate. Call on a couple students to share a reason before revealing the next message."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "345e2fbf-afae-4447-b70d-a04705d78ef8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0f5060bc-7c42-4c4e-a600-4925b782bdec",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the third message aloud, then have students vote by hand signal: approve, override, or escalate. Call on a couple students to share a reason before revealing the next message.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Watch for students overriding this one out of habit from the last two messages. If most of the class overrides it, pause here rather than waiting for the pattern slide, and ask what is actually different about this sender."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0f5060bc-7c42-4c4e-a600-4925b782bdec",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5395fb9c-c301-4259-9647-3f9188b65a2d",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the final message aloud, then have students vote by hand signal: approve, override, or escalate. Call on a couple students to share a reason before moving to the discussion."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5395fb9c-c301-4259-9647-3f9188b65a2d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "dfa23007-55a8-405a-8df2-f3406f34a0b7",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *What do you notice about the messages you overrode? Is there a pattern?*\n- *What does the bot actually need?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that every override involved a veteran member using slang the bot was never trained on, while the one real problem came from a brand-new account — no need for the term \"model drift\" yet. On the fix, guide them to see that retraining alone or adjusting the model alone won't work; the bot needs new data that includes this community's slang, then needs to be retrained on it."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "dfa23007-55a8-405a-8df2-f3406f34a0b7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "12829413-cccc-47fe-9ff1-5c7ddbcf1e64",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "12829413-cccc-47fe-9ff1-5c7ddbcf1e64",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "fe65ae0a-b176-4d7d-9ec3-c842666cfc97",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "fe65ae0a-b176-4d7d-9ec3-c842666cfc97",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1c0c4e16-5c0c-4441-8c42-4078ca13e779"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b71f8bbe-d9f5-478d-8a1a-159b0280744c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students name what they just experienced in the warm-up — model drift — then build the vocabulary and toolkit (the four ways things can go wrong, the four possible actions) they'll need to diagnose and respond to events during today's simulation.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to take out their Unit 1 Unit Guide.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Build Your Toolkit"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b71f8bbe-d9f5-478d-8a1a-159b0280744c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2968d58f-a49a-47fa-9e81-6493e7da7cab",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define model drift. Point back to the Auto-Mod bot from the warm-up — its accuracy on veteran members using new slang is drift in action. Have students record the definition in their Unit Guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2968d58f-a49a-47fa-9e81-6493e7da7cab",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "15f1c166-8ffb-44a7-830e-a9696a9b1f22",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define each of the four categories. Tell students these are the four things they'll need to diagnose during today's activity.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Don't preview which action fixes each category — figuring that out themselves is the point of Keep It Running. This slide should name the four problems, not the four solutions."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "15f1c166-8ffb-44a7-830e-a9696a9b1f22",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "031b99ae-882d-4479-812b-33594b418fc2",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that a model can't catch its own drift. A human monitoring performance is what catches it, and a human decides how to respond.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Point back to two moments students already experienced: in the warm-up, the bot never noticed its own pattern of mistakes — a human (them) had to catch it. In \"Catching Drift Takes a Human,\" it's the same idea, just named as a standard: humans are the ones who monitor, and humans are the ones who decide what happens next."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "031b99ae-882d-4479-812b-33594b418fc2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a4056aa4-e49b-4600-9dac-a85cb1cbb96d",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *transparency statement*. Have students record the definition in their Unit Guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a4056aa4-e49b-4600-9dac-a85cb1cbb96d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d3b10a66-13c6-498e-8713-ef24317c50a1",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Use the slide to tell students that an AI system at launch is not the same system a year later. Tell them they're about to spend a year finding out exactly what that means.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "This is the moment to make explicit that students are about to be the human choice this slide describes — every action they take in the simulation is one of the differences between their system at launch and their system a year later."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d3b10a66-13c6-498e-8713-ef24317c50a1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "61f4feb5-98a6-4590-9a40-c2938b5b583d",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the four actions students will choose between during today's simulation. Do not tell students which action fixes which type of problem — figuring that out is the point of the activity."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "61f4feb5-98a6-4590-9a40-c2938b5b583d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "396b1e7d-0122-4420-bd4f-4b464144f33f",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students diagnose what's happening to their AI system and choose how to respond, then connect that experience back to the warm-up and to real AI systems they actually use during the debrief.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Pair students up before starting. Partners work through Level 1 together, discussing each event and deciding how to respond as a team.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 14, Levels 1 to complete Level 1 with their partner. Students should complete Level 2 individually.\n- **Level 1:** Students go through four rounds of the simulation. Each round is one of the four ways things can go wrong.\n- **Level 2:** Students complete a check for understanding.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Watch for justifications that don't actually explain the reasoning (a single word, or a restatement of the action) — ask pairs to say their reasoning out loud before typing it. Also watch for pairs clicking \"Skip\" on a stale transparency statement field without noticing why it's flagged.",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Keep It Running",
        "progression_name": "Keep It Running",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "An optional Activity Guide is available for Level 1. It isn't required — experiencing the simulation is meant to be a learning experience, not a formative assessment. If you'd like students to turn in evidence of their work, you can distribute the activity guide to students which gives them two options: screenshot the Year in Review summary screen, or copy and paste the summary text."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Level 2 checks all three lesson objectives. The Decision That Mattered checks that students can name a real human decision from their own gameplay and its effect — the core of the standard. Spot the Drift checks whether they can recognize model drift in a new scenario and explain how humans should respond. What Users Deserve to Know checks whether they can describe what a transparency statement must include and why it matters to users."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "396b1e7d-0122-4420-bd4f-4b464144f33f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "51a9d105-9bf2-444c-80d8-8616389bd2bb",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click the animated slide to display the discussion prompts.\n- *Where did you see the same kind of mistake happen in both the warm-up and the simulation — a system getting something wrong because the world around it changed, not because it was broken?*\n- *Where have you seen this happen in a real AI system you've actually used?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Guide students to name the shared thread explicitly: in the warm-up, the bot misread messages because gaming slang had shifted beyond what it was trained on; in the simulation, at least one event (drift or usage shift) put their system in the same position — right at launch, wrong once the world moved. The system in both cases wasn't \"broken,\" it just hadn't caught up. For the second question, listen for real examples like a recommendation algorithm missing a new trend, a spam filter missing new scam wording, or a voice assistant struggling with an accent or slang it wasn't trained on — the specific example matters less than whether students can correctly identify it as the same pattern: real-world change outpacing what a system was built to handle."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "51a9d105-9bf2-444c-80d8-8616389bd2bb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e418905a-5d47-46c1-bccc-7fdfa990949e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "288eb784-a170-4cf2-b26a-429c50c2f2f5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "288eb784-a170-4cf2-b26a-429c50c2f2f5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "f6de41ec-03e2-4fe8-882c-99335f62b73f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "22462a03-0c3e-444c-9a24-e7037796eb69",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day. Give students thirty seconds to write one word on scrap paper, a sticky note, or the back of their Unit Guide that answers the Question of the Day. On your count of three, everyone holds their word up at once.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Scan the room as words go up. Call out three or four that capture the lesson well, and briefly address any that reveal a misunderstanding before moving on."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "22462a03-0c3e-444c-9a24-e7037796eb69",
        "lesson_activity.key": "f6de41ec-03e2-4fe8-882c-99335f62b73f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "88071db8-a4b8-4cf9-a54b-20e54ccc78dc",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "88071db8-a4b8-4cf9-a54b-20e54ccc78dc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "f6de41ec-03e2-4fe8-882c-99335f62b73f"
      }
    },
